reconstructed_question:
Find the smallest positive integer $x$ satisfying the following system of congruences:
$$
\begin{cases}
x \equiv 11 \pmod{36} \\
x \equiv 7 \pmod{40} \\
x \equiv 11 \pmod{75}
\end{cases}
$$
Note: The third congruence uses the same residue as the first ($x \equiv 11 \pmod{75}$). How does this specific choice of congruences lead to the solution $x=407$?
